      "text": "14,833 + 4,694 + 0,657 = 20,184.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me try a different approach. I'll multiply 186 by 200, which is 37,200. Then, I'll multiply 186 by 36, giving me 6,696. Adding these two results together, 37,200 + 6,696 equals 43,896. That makes more sense.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **186** and **236**, follow these easy steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Multiplication\nWe'll use the standard multiplication method by breaking down **236** into smaller, more manageable parts.\n\n\\[\n236 = 200 + 30 + 6\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part Separately\nNow, multiply **186** by each of these parts:\n\n1. **Multiply by 200:**\n   \\[\n   186 \\times 200 = 37,\\!200\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply by 30:**\n   \\[\n   186 \\times 30 = 5,\\!580\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply by 6:**\n   \\[\n   186 \\times 6 = 1,\\!116\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Results Together\nNow, add the three products obtained:\n\n\\[\n37,\\!200 + 5,\\!580 + 1,\\!116 = 43,\\!896\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{43,\\!896}\n\\]",
