  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "145,117.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **748** and **897**, we'll use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{000}748 \\\\\n\\times\\phantom{000}897 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 748 by 7\n\\[\n748 \\times 7 = 5,236\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 748 by 90 (which is 9 tens)\n\\[\n748 \\times 90 = 748 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 6,732 \\times 10 = 67,320\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 748 by 800 (which is 8 hundreds)\n\\[\n748 \\times 800 = 748 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 5,984 \\times 100 = 598,400\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add all the results together\n\\[\n5,236 + 67,320 + 598,400 = 671,956\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{671,\\!956}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
      "prompt_logprobs": null
    }
