      "index": 0,
      "text": "237,899 minus 8,193 equals 229,706.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **647** and **596**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe'll use the **distributive property** to simplify the multiplication.\n\n\\[\n647 \\times 596 = 647 \\times (500 + 90 + 6)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part Separately\nCalculate each part of the sum separately.\n\n1. **Multiply 647 by 500:**\n   \\[\n   647 \\times 500 = 323,\\!500\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 647 by 90:**\n   \\[\n   647 \\times 90 = 58,\\!230\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 647 by 6:**\n   \\[\n   647 \\times 6 = 3,\\!882\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Results Together\nNow, sum up all the products obtained from the previous step.\n\n\\[\n323,\\!500 + 58,\\!230 + 3,\\!882 = 385,\\!612\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{385,\\!612}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
      "prompt_logprobs": null
    }
