      "text": "091,727 - 07,586 = 084,141.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me double-check my calculations.\n\nActually, I think I made a mistake in breaking down the numbers. Let me try a different approach.\n\nI'll start by multiplying 530 by 976 directly. Breaking it down:\n\n530 multiplied by 900 is 477,000.\n\n530 multiplied by 70 is 37,100.\n\n530 multiplied by 6 is 3,180.\n\nAdding these together: 477,000 + 37,100 = 514,100.\n\nThen, 514,100 + 3,180 = 517,280.\n\nSo, the correct product of 530 and 976 is 517,280.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **530** and **976**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n   \n   \\[\n   530 \\times 976 = 530 \\times (900 + 70 + 6)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 530 by each component:**\n   \n   - **530 \u00d7 900:**\n     \n     \\[\n     530 \\times 900 = 477,\\!000\n     \\]\n   \n   - **530 \u00d7 70:**\n     \n     \\[\n     530 \\times 70 = 37,\\!100\n     \\]\n   \n   - **530 \u00d7 6:**\n     \n     \\[\n     530 \\times 6 = 3,\\!180\n     \\]\n\n3. **Add the results together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   477,\\!000 + 37,\\!100 + 3,\\!180 = 517,\\!280\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{517,\\!280}\n\\]",
