      "text": "705,023 minus 2 equals 705,021.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **983** and **979**, we can use the **difference of squares** method for easier calculation. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n983 \\times 979 &= (981 + 2)(981 - 2) \\\\\n&= 981^2 - 2^2 \\quad \\text{(Using the identity } (a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2) \\\\\n&= 962,361 - 4 \\\\\n&= 962,357\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{962,\\!357}\n\\]",
