      "text": "60,398 + 51,042 + 958 = 112,400.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me double-check my calculations.\n\nActually, I made a mistake in my initial approach. The correct way is to multiply 183 by 373 directly. Breaking it down:\n\n183 multiplied by 300 is 54,900.\n\n183 multiplied by 70 is 12,810.\n\n183 multiplied by 3 is 549.\n\nAdding these together: 54,900 + 12,810 + 549 equals 68,259.\n\nSo, the correct product of 183 and 373 is 68,259.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **183** and **373**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   183 \\times 373 = 183 \\times (300 + 70 + 3)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply each part separately:**\n\n   - **Multiply 183 by 300:**\n     \\[\n     183 \\times 300 = 54,\\!900\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Multiply 183 by 70:**\n     \\[\n     183 \\times 70 = 12,\\!810\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Multiply 183 by 3:**\n     \\[\n     183 \\times 3 = 549\n     \\]\n\n3. **Add all the results together:**\n\n   \\[\n   54,\\!900 + 12,\\!810 + 549 = 68,\\!259\n   \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{68,\\!259}\n   \\]",
