  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "49,921.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **202** and **290**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 202 by 290:**\n\n   \\[\n   202 \\times 290\n   \\]\n\n2. **Break down the multiplication for simplicity:**\n\n   \\[\n   202 \\times 290 = 202 \\times (200 + 90) = (202 \\times 200) + (202 \\times 90)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate each part separately:**\n\n   - **First part:**\n     \\[\n     202 \\times 200 = 40,\\!400\n     \\]\n     \n   - **Second part:**\n     \\[\n     202 \\times 90 = 18,\\!180\n     \\]\n\n4. **Add the two results together:**\n\n   \\[\n   40,\\!400 + 18,\\!180 = 58,\\!580\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{58,\\!580}\n   \\]",
