      "index": 0,
      "text": "09,850.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **355** and **375**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nLet's break down **355** and **375** into smaller, more manageable parts.\n\n\\[\n355 = 300 + 50 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\n375 = 300 + 70 + 5\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\nNow, multiply each part of **355** by each part of **375**.\n\n1. **Multiply 300 by 300:**\n   \\[\n   300 \\times 300 = 90,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 300 by 70:**\n   \\[\n   300 \\times 70 = 21,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 300 by 5:**\n   \\[\n   300 \\times 5 = 1,\\!500\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply 50 by 300:**\n   \\[\n   50 \\times 300 = 15,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply 50 by 70:**\n   \\[\n   50 \\times 70 = 3,\\!500\n   \\]\n\n6. **Multiply 50 by 5:**\n   \\[\n   50 \\times 5 = 250\n   \\]\n\n7. **Multiply 5 by 300:**\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 300 = 1,\\!500\n   \\]\n\n8. **Multiply 5 by 70:**\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 70 = 350\n   \\]\n\n9. **Multiply 5 by 5:**\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 5 = 25\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\nNow, sum all the results from the previous step:\n\n\\[\n90,\\!000 + 21,\\!000 + 1,\\!500 + 15,\\!000 + 3,\\!500 + 250 + 1,\\!500 + 350 + 25 = 133,\\!125\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{133,\\!125}\n\\]",
